      "prerequisites": ["Python 3.8+, Git, and a writable canonical project root with no link or reparse ancestors.", "Current installed-clone catalog and definition evidence, plus valid strict project config and active manifest or recognized no-config legacy installation evidence.", "In Git projects, .compound-gpid/runtime/help-requests files must be untracked and ignored; cg-link manages the runtime ignore entry."],
      "outputs": ["Schema-v1 JSON transport envelopes on stdout, with deterministic Markdown inside semantic results.", "Prepared request UUID and confined query path; candidate results prepare a selection path for allowed command IDs.", "Overview, exact command, candidates, documented workflow, unsupported, or error results; nonzero CLI errors also emit stderr diagnostics."],
      "constraints": ["Choose exactly one operation. Write UTF-8 query text in place to the returned query file through a structured file-write tool; never pass query text as a shell argument.", "Use the returned UUID and the same project root, platform, catalog, and source-root binding for consume and render operations.", "Query input is limited to 4096 bytes; selection input is a JSON array of at most three distinct allowed command IDs, limited to 1024 bytes. Requests and selections are single-use and expire after 300 seconds.", "Only candidates permit selection rendering. Write the selection array in place to the returned selection file; changed catalog or project evidence requires a new request.", "--catalog and --source-root are paired local fixture overrides, not normal catalog selection flags.", "CLI exit categories are 0 success, 2 invalid transport or input, 3 invalid evidence, and 4 filesystem or I/O failure; missing Python makes the wrapper exit 1."],
      "relatedCommands": [{"id": "shell:cg-link", "relation": "related"}],
